15 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Conceptual flowchart titled \215Evidence-ranked model linking therapy pressure, lineage plasticity, microenvironmental remodeling, and therapeutic vulnerabilities.\216 Boxes with arrows depict relationships among therapy pressure, NEPC state, tumor microenvironment remodeling components \(immune TME, stromal niche, vascular-hypoxic axis, metabolic-epigenetic cues\), candidate clinical associations, candidate mediators, and intervention domains. Text details specific factors involved in each component.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating cellular interactions within the NEPC tumor microenvironment, including exhausted CD8+ T cells, Tregs, CAFs, suppressive TAMs, and MDSCs, each secreting factors that drive immune suppression, vascular and ECM remodeling, angiogenesis, and metastatic niche formation. Legend identifies icons for immune suppression, ECM/fibrosis, hypoxia/angiogenesis, and metastatic niche.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Infographic illustrating candidate tumor microenvironment-associated mechanisms for neuroendocrine differentiation and lineage plasticity in prostate cancer, highlighting cytokine signaling, extracellular matrix remodeling, hypoxia, vascular remodeling, and metabolic or epigenetic programs influencing transformation to therapy-resistant neuroendocrine prostate cancer cells.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Graphic illustrating candidate tumor microenvironment \(TME\) mechanisms of therapy resistance in neuroendocrine prostate cancer \(NEPC\). Panels detail immune, chemotherapy, and targeted therapy resistance mechanisms, ending with a progression timeline from reduced response to short-lived control and ultimately progressive disease with tumor regrowth and spread.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Infographic outlining therapeutic opportunities in neuroendocrine prostate cancer and the tumor microenvironment, showing three tiers: Tier 1 current clinical backbone, Tier 2 emerging NEPC-directed strategies, and Tier 3 investigational TME-directed strategies, with a process flow for biomarker selection, combination therapy, and response monitoring; a caution notes varying evidence maturity, with many TME strategies in preclinical or early clinical stages.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
